course: dictionary
lesson: 14405
title: Reading the sky: overcast
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Overcast is a word about the sky. When the sky is overcast, it is covered with grey clouds and you cannot see the sun. «The sky was overcast all morning, so we never saw the sun.» The clues are grey clouds and no sun, so overcast must mean covered with clouds.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence: «The sky was covered with grey clouds all morning, so we never saw the sun.» It still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
explain: Weather reports use overcast too. «Tomorrow will be cool and overcast, with no rain expected.» An overcast day is dull and grey, but it does not have to be wet. Do not think overcast always means rain.
explain: Writers use a grey, overcast sky to set a mood. «The overcast sky made the village feel gloomy and quiet.» When you see a sky like this in a story, expect the mood to be grey and a bit sad.
fact: Overcast is an adjective: «an overcast sky» describes the sky.
fact: Overcast means covered with grey clouds, so the sun cannot be seen.
fact: In a weather report, overcast means dull and grey, but not necessarily rainy.
fact: Weather words, from least to most cloud, include clear, partly cloudy, cloudy and overcast.
fact: Writers often use «an overcast sky» to make a story feel gloomy.
exercise: «The sky was overcast, so the sun never came out.» What does overcast mean? | Very windy | Bright and sunny | *Covered with grey clouds | Full of stars
exercise: Weather report: «Today will be overcast but dry.» Does overcast mean it will rain? | It means the sun is very hot | *Not necessarily, it can be grey and still dry | Yes, it will pour all day | It means the wind is very strong
exercise: In a weather list (clear, partly cloudy, cloudy, overcast), which word means the sky has no clouds? | Overcast | Partly cloudy | Cloudy | *Clear
test: «The overcast sky made the park look grey and sad.» What does overcast mean here? | Covered with bright stars | Clear and cloudless | *Covered with grey clouds | Full of colourful flowers
test: Which picture matches an overcast day? | A rainbow after the rain | Bright sun in a blue sky | A night full of stars | *A grey sky with no sun showing
exam: Ruby says overcast always means rainy. Is she right? | Yes, overcast always means rain | *No, it means covered with grey clouds, and the day can stay dry | Overcast means the sun is shining brightly | Overcast means very hot
